     Strings of the alpha notice (issue #199), shown on aerie://setup and on About (Settings). The setup page
     lists them in aerie_onboarding_localized_strings.h; patches/branding/0007 hands them to Settings.
     tests/test_alpha_notice.py checks both. -->
<grit-part>
  <message name="IDS_AERIE_ALPHA_NOTICE" desc="Notice on the setup page and on About that Aerie is early software and has not been audited by an outside party.">
    Aerie is alpha software and has not had an independent security audit.
  </message>
  <message name="IDS_AERIE_ALPHA_TERMS_LINK" desc="Link text next to the alpha notice. The link opens Aerie's terms of use.">
    Terms of use
  </message>
  <message name="IDS_AERIE_ALPHA_PRIVACY_LINK" desc="Link text next to the alpha notice. The link opens Aerie's privacy policy.">
    Privacy policy
  </message>
</grit-part>
